  "description": "Preparing a roux with butter and sweet rice flour produces a gluten-free gravy that's delicious and silky smooth.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: low-sodium chicken → turkey stock or skimmed pan drippings\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Gravy can be made up to 2 days in advance and refrigerated in an airtight container. Reheat in a saucepan on low heat, adding stock as needed to loosen, until warmed through. Gravy can also be made several hours ahead and kept warm in a slow cooker until ready to serve.",
